      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>

  <xs:simpleType name="adc_saturated_pixel_count">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:adc_saturated_pixel_count provides a
        count of the number of pixels where the analog-to-digital
        converter (ADC) was saturated. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_NonNegative_Integer">
    	<xs:pattern value='[0-9]+'/>
     <xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="18446744073709551615"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="bad_pixel_count">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:bad_pixel_count attribute provides a
        count of the number of bad pixels as identified by the Deep
        Impact calibration process. This count includes any VIS
        overclock pixels or IR reference pixels at the borders of the
        image. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_NonNegative_Integer">
    	<xs:pattern value='[0-9]+'/>
     <xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="18446744073709551615"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="commanded_image_count">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:commanded_image_count provides the
        number of images intended to be acquired acquired by the imaging
        command that resulted in the associated data product.
        </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Integer">
     <xs:minInclusive value="1"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="9223372036854775807"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="data_to_calibrated_dn_multiplier">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:data_to_calibrated_dn_multipler provides
        the scaling factor for converting the image data from the
        currently specified unit to calibrated data numbers (DN), before
        the conversion to radiance units. A value of 1 indicates the
        current image is already in units of raw data number.
        </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Real">
     <xs:minInclusive value="-1.7976931348623157e308"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="1.7976931348623157e308"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="data_to_ioverf_multiplier">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:data_to_ioverf_multiplier provides the
        scaling factor for converting the image data from the currently
        specified unit to unitless I-over-F data. A value of 1 indicates
        the current image is already in units of I-over-F.
        </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Real">
     <xs:minInclusive value="-1.7976931348623157e308"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="1.7976931348623157e308"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="data_to_radiance_multiplier">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:data_to_radiance_multiplier provides the
        scaling factor for converting the image data from the currently
        specified unit to radiance data, W/(m**2*micron*sr). A value of
        1 indicates the current image is already in units of radiance.
        </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Real">
     <xs:minInclusive value="-1.7976931348623157e308"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="1.7976931348623157e308"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="despiked_pixel_count">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:despiked_pixel_count provides a count of
        the number of pixels that were modified by the despiking routine
        in the calibration pipeline. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_NonNegative_Integer">
    	<xs:pattern value='[0-9]+'/>
     <xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="18446744073709551615"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="geometry_quality">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:geometry_quality_flag indicates the
        quality of the calculated geometric parameters. A value of BAD
        indicates some or all values could not be calculated or the
        values may not be accurate and should be used with caution.
        </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="255"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="image_compression_history">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:image_compression_history attribute
        indicates whether the associated iamge data were compressed
        aboard the spacecraft, and if so, whether they are still in that
        compressed state. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="255"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="image_number">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:image_number provides the sequential
        number for an image within an observation. For EPOXI data,
        multiple images could have been associated with a single
        di:observation_id. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Integer">
     <xs:minInclusive value="1"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="9223372036854775807"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="instrument_mode">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:instrument_mode attribute provides the
        human-readable expansion of the di:instrument_mode_mnemonic
        field, and corresponds to the di:instrument_mode_id for the
        particular instrument. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="255"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="instrument_mode_id">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:instrument_mode_id is a number
        indicating the operating mode of the instrument during the
        associated observation. It corresponds to the
        instrument_mode_mnemonic and the instrument_mode. Instrument
        modes for the CCD instruments (HRIV, MRI, and ITS) are all the
        same. The HRII spectrometer has its own set of modes.
        </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Integer">
     <xs:minInclusive value="1"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="9"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="instrument_mode_mnemonic">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:instrument_mode_mnemonic corresponds to
        the di:instrument_mode_id and the di:instrument_mode, which
        should also be present. The CCD instruments (HTIV, MRI, and ITS)
        all use the same set of mode IDs, mnemonics, and names. The HRII
        spectrometer has its own set. The instrument modes were
        identical for primary and extended missions. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="255"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="interpolated_pixel_count">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:interpolated_pixel_count provides a
        count of the number of pixels that were reclaimed, in the
        calibration pipeline, by interpolating from the values of
        neighgboring good pixels. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_NonNegative_Integer">
    	<xs:pattern value='[0-9]+'/>
     <xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="18446744073709551615"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="missing_pixel_count">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:missing_pixel_count provides a count of
        the number of pixels that were not received from the spacecraft
        and pixels that are the image header bytes. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_NonNegative_Integer">
    	<xs:pattern value='[0-9]+'/>
     <xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="18446744073709551615"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="mission_activity">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:mission_activity attribute provides a
        human-readable tag for the context of an observation (for
        example, "Daily Science Imaging"). </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="255"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="mission_phase_name">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:mission_phase_name is the name of a
        specific mission phase, as defined in the mission documentation.
        </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="255"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="observation_description">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:observation_description provides a
        brief, human-readable description elucidating the
        di:observation_id value. This corresponds to the PDS3 keyword
        OBSERVATION_TYPE. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="255"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="observation_id">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:observation_id is a numeric string
        identifying a specific calibration-related or scientific
        observation. A single 'observation' may consist of more than one
        image (the di:image_number provides the sequence number within
        the observation for a specific image). In the EPOXI missions, a
        calibration sequence was often reused, so that the same
        observation_id might appear more than once within a data
        collection. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="7"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="partial_saturated_pixel_count">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:partial_saturated_pixel_count provides a
        count of the number of pixels where the raw DN value is above
        the point where some pixels have reached partial saturation. For
        the VIS CCD instruments this point occurs at 11,000 raw DN and
        at 8,000 raw DN for the HRII IR spectrometer. </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_NonNegative_Integer">
    	<xs:pattern value='[0-9]+'/>
     <xs:minInclusive value="0"/>
     <xs:maxInclusive value="18446744073709551615"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="pointing_description">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:pointing_desc provides the planned
        spacecraft pointing as described in an imaging sequence.
        </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="pds:ASCII_Short_String_Collapsed">
     <xs:minLength value="1"/>
     <xs:maxLength value="255"/>
	   </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <xs:simpleType name="product_type">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation> The di:product_type attribute provides a
        categorization for the data product based on its state of
